Usages:
  soft_delete_by_default: |
    Deleting a thread in the everyday sense never removes its database row: the deletion
    contract wipes the thread's interactions and associated per-thread state (pins, intents,
    associated data) but keeps the thread row itself so it can be recreated/resurfaced.
    Only a small set of special cases (terminated groups, private story threads) proceed to
    an actual row removal.
  transaction_scoped_access: |
    Every read, write, or deletion operation exposed by this cell's types takes an explicit
    read or write transaction token; there is no ambient mutable thread state.

Annotations: |
  This cell owns the lifecycle of conversation threads: looking them up, updating their
  per-thread associated data, and deleting/removing them. It is deliberately narrow — actual
  interaction deletion is delegated to a separate contract this cell's deletion manager
  coordinates with internally, not re-exposed here.
  Use `soft_delete_by_default` for `ThreadDeletionManager`.
  Use `transaction_scoped_access` for every method on this cell's types.

---

"ThreadDeletionManager()":
  location: ThreadDeletionManager.swift
  annotations: |
    Coordinates the user-facing notion of "deleting" one or more threads.

    Use `soft_delete_by_default` for the overall deletion algorithm.
    Use `transaction_scoped_access` for both methods below.
  methods:
    "deleteThreads(threads: [TSGroupThread], sendDeleteForMeSyncMessage: Bool, updateStorageService: Bool, localIdentifiers: String, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Deletes the given threads' content and, for eligible thread kinds, the thread rows
      themselves.

      `threads`: the threads to delete
      `sendDeleteForMeSyncMessage`: whether to notify linked devices of this deletion
      `updateStorageService`: whether to also propagate the deletion to Storage Service

      Algorithm:
      1. For each thread, remove all of its interactions per `soft_delete_by_default`.
      2. Unpin the thread and remove any associated Siri/Intents data.
      3. If the thread kind is eligible for hard deletion (a terminated group, or a private
         story thread), remove the thread row itself; otherwise leave the row in place.
      4. If `sendDeleteForMeSyncMessage` is set, notify linked devices of the deletion.
    "removeAllInteractions(thread: TSGroupThread, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Removes every interaction belonging to `thread` without removing the thread row itself.

"ThreadStore()":
  location: ThreadStore.swift
  annotations: |
    Read/update data-access contract over persisted threads and their per-thread associated
    data (archived/muted/marked-unread state, playback rate).

    Use `transaction_scoped_access` for every method below.
  methods:
    "fetchThread(uniqueId: String, tx: DBReadTransaction) -> thread: TSGroupThread?": |
      Looks up a thread by its stable identifier.
    "fetchContactThreads(phoneNumber: String, tx: DBReadTransaction) -> threads: [String]": |
      Returns the one-on-one contact threads associated with the given phone number.
    "getOrCreateContactThread(address: String, tx: DBWriteTransaction) -> thread: String": |
      Returns the existing one-on-one thread for `address`, creating it first if absent.
    "removeThread(thread: TSGroupThread, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Deletes the thread row itself. Called only by the deletion manager for eligible cases.
    "updateThread(thread: TSGroupThread, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Persists in-memory changes made to `thread`.
    "updateAssociatedData(threadUniqueId: String, isArchived: Bool?, isMarkedUnread: Bool?, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Updates the per-thread associated-data flags (archived/unread) for the given thread.

"TSGroupThread()":
  location: TSGroupThread.swift
  annotations: |
    The persisted thread subtype backing a group conversation; one-to-one with a group's
    versioned model and membership state.
  properties:
    "uniqueId -> String": |
      Stable identifier for this thread row, shared with the interactions it owns.
    "groupId -> Data": |
      The group identifier this thread represents.

"TSContactThread()":
  location: TSContactThread.swift
  annotations: |
    The persisted thread subtype backing a one-on-one conversation with a single contact.
  properties:
    "uniqueId -> String": |
      Stable identifier for this thread row.

